{"authorID": 6835922, "authorType": 0, "children": [], "childrenTotalCount": 0, "commentID": 3843837, "commentThreadID": 220961, "createdAt": "2021-07-10T18:25:15Z", "editedAt": "2021-07-10T18:25:15Z", "isDeleted": false, "isHidden": false, "isReportedByCreator": false, "likesCount": 1, "newerChildrenCount": 0, "newRepliesCount": 0, "parentID": null, "pinnedAt": null, "text": "For anyone considering buying this - do not.  It's only marginally better than manual focus, and it IS NOT for continuous autofocus.

the unit "jumps" to each focal point that you've set, so for things like sports or moving the camera, it's completely useless.

The DJI lidar autofocus is continuous and smooth and doesn't require the ridiculous setup this thing requires.  Don't waste your money.", "userComment": null}

{"authorID": 6835922, "authorType": 0, "children": [], "childrenTotalCount": 0, "commentID": 3843834, "commentThreadID": 220961, "createdAt": "2021-06-03T21:15:14Z", "editedAt": "2021-06-03T21:15:14Z", "isDeleted": false, "isHidden": false, "isReportedByCreator": false, "likesCount": 0, "newerChildrenCount": 0, "newRepliesCount": 0, "parentID": null, "pinnedAt": null, "text": "is anyone else having a nightmare of a time getting their unit to work *at all*?  

I've been following their directions precisely and yet still can't press the D button on my R1 to calibrate a lens. Even though I initialize the R1, it doesn't appear to work.

CDA, this is another reason why requiring the R1 to operate is a stupid requirement.", "userComment": null}
